cuFFT input-placement ladder: WRITE + TRANSFORM
build: 6070ae1   5 reps x 9 arms x 9 sizes, arms interleaved per iteration

Why both halves are reported:
  In the pipeline benchmark the producer's write happens OUTSIDE the
  measured window.  A change that makes the write slower and the
  transform faster would therefore look like a pure win while being
  neutral or worse in reality.  Reporting the transform alone would be
  a stopwatch artifact, so write, transform and their total are all
  below and the verdict is taken on the TOTAL.

Decision rule, fixed before the data exists:
  Reading from device memory was worth 6.10 us at 4 MB in the earlier
  read-only ladder (47.55 vs 53.66).  So if landing data in device
  memory costs MORE than 6.10 us of extra write time, the direction is
  dead and no implementation route gets started.

Note on the 'device' arm: it reaches device memory the only way it
  normally can, by copying.  Its write column is a full H2D transfer.
  'devwrite' is the one that matters: the data LANDS there.

